<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The V-Bombers (No AC Dmg)</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The Royal Air Force's V-Bomber Force against the Soviet Union, August 1962&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;You are Commander in Chief, Bomber Command and responsible for the United Kingdom's nuclear deterrent forces of Victor and Vulcan bombers and the American made&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;PGM-17 Thor&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; Intermediate Range Ballistic Missiles (IRBM). For whatever reason, deterrence has failed and a full-scale nuclear exchange with the Soviet Union and its allies has begun.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Background&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Initially the RAF's intended&amp;nbsp;nuclear forces consisted of piston-engine Avro Lincolns and Boeing&amp;nbsp;B-29 Washingtons the latter acquired from the United States but the 1946 Atomic Energy Act (aka the McMahon Act) excluded Britain from accessing American nuclear knowhow. Anticipating&amp;nbsp;the development&amp;nbsp;of indigenous nuclear weapons and&amp;nbsp;with the advanced state of the British aviation industry the production of&amp;nbsp;effective jet bombers was practically a given. Long before &lt;STRONG&gt;Operation Hurricane&lt;/STRONG&gt; demonstrated a British fission device, proposals and specifications were sent by the Air Ministry to the big British aircraft manufacturers.&amp;nbsp;The Short Sperrin from 1951 was a&amp;nbsp;flop but Vickers, Handley-Page and A.V. Roe&amp;nbsp;responded with&amp;nbsp;the Valiant, Victor and Vulcan bombers respectively. First to deploy were the Valiants and some of these actually dropped live&amp;nbsp;weapons during nuclear tests and saw conventional combat in the Suez Crisis&amp;nbsp;and Malaya but the aircraft was a conservative design and suffered from structural problems. By 1962 the Valiants had lost their combat role and were used exclusively as tankers.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Far more sophisticated were the Handley-Page Victor and the delta-wing Avro Vulcan but there were issues with the weapons that they would carry. British nuclear weapon production was limited; designs&amp;nbsp;lacked miniaturization&amp;nbsp;and political problems prevented Bomber Command from deploying stand-off weapons while production of gravity bombs was slow.&amp;nbsp;Shortages of British-made weapons caused the&amp;nbsp;Eisenhower administration&amp;nbsp;to suspend the McMahon Act in 1957 and provide initially &lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mk-5&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; boosted fission and later&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;Mk-28&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;staged thermonuclear&amp;nbsp;free-fall weapons (represented in this scenario by the British&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;WE.177&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; as there&amp;nbsp;are no &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;Mk-28&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; loadouts for the V-Bombers and none of the &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;WE.177&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; family were ready in 1962) and some Victors&amp;nbsp;were modified to deliver them. The British produced &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Yellow Sun&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; was a 1-megaton (MT) city-busting weapon and a true staged thermonuclear device but the 15-kiloton (KT) &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Red Beard&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; was an unboosted fission bomb that had a very small yield by 1962 standards, even if it was the most numerous British-made nuclear gravity bomb at this time.&amp;nbsp;The attack plans called for fast, high-altitude penetration of Soviet airspace and the bombers' only defences were their state of the art electronic-warfare suites and the agility of the big four-engine jets.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Bomber Command was&amp;nbsp;coordinated&amp;nbsp;with the US SIOP-63 and the RAF's target lists prioritized Soviet strategic weapon bases (Alpha targets) and&amp;nbsp;urban/industrial centres&amp;nbsp;(Charlie targets) as it was clear that British cities would be targets of any Russian nuclear strikes. The RAF never had the political clout or resources of America's Strategic Air Command so maintaining more than one bomber per squadron on alert (Quick Reaction Alert or QRA&amp;nbsp;in RAF jargon); that is fueled, with a dedicated ready crew&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;ready at less than 15-minutes notice, proved impractical. In the event of increasing tensions, the V-Bombers&amp;nbsp;could disperse throughout Great Britain&amp;nbsp;in a QRA&amp;nbsp;posture for a limited time but in this scenario we have cycled from peace to war too fast to redeploy&amp;nbsp;and are still at&amp;nbsp;peacetime readiness. However, nine dispersal bases have been allocated to your command&amp;nbsp;but without&amp;nbsp;pre-positioned nuclear weapons. Your authorized targets in the Western Soviet Union are shown on the map and the RAF&amp;nbsp;Target List.rtf file included but your information may be incomplete and targets of opportunity may be located as operations unfold.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The RAF deployed 60 &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;I&gt;PGM-17 Thor&lt;/I&gt; &lt;/STRONG&gt;missiles at bases&amp;nbsp;near the east coast. Never popular with Bomber Command,&amp;nbsp;about half were theoretically&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;QRA at any one time but&amp;nbsp;&lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thor&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; proved cranky in service and it was very difficult to reliably achieve the&amp;nbsp;QRA launch requirements despite the best efforts of their well-trained crews.&amp;nbsp;Largely unwanted by&amp;nbsp;the RAF, the &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thors&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; would disappear&amp;nbsp;when the United States offered &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;Polaris&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; to the UK. In this scenario, the missiles will&amp;nbsp;ready at&amp;nbsp;random times via Lua scripts. Some&amp;nbsp;may actually be ready to fire&amp;nbsp;close to&amp;nbsp;the 15-minute time frame. One missile was used solely for training and so 59 were theoretically available at any one time.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;In 1962&amp;nbsp;there were American B-52s based in Britain; SAC's forward deployments&amp;nbsp;as part of&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;Operation Reflex Action&lt;/STRONG&gt; but they have their own orders and targets and are beyond your control so they do not appear in the scenario. Likewise Bomber Command had quantities of the English Electric Canberra medium bombers&amp;nbsp;with a nuclear role but for our purposes, all are employed in a tactical support role in Europe and are also absent.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;In the event of a full-scale nuclear attack the Home Office anticipated millions of&amp;nbsp;casualties initially and the V-Bomber crews could be pretty certain that if they returned at all, it would be to an irradiated wasteland with their families probably dead and&amp;nbsp;the British Isles&amp;nbsp;in ruins. But nobody should have any doubt that in spite of the&amp;nbsp;likely outcome, Bomber Command's crews would have acquitted themselves well had the unthinkable become reality.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Scenario Designer's Notes&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;When I first uploaded &lt;EM&gt;Wargasm 1962&lt;/EM&gt; I had wanted to follow it up with a scenario involving the RAF's V-Bomber force. Over four-years and more than 100-CMANO builds later with perhaps a dozen iterations of the scenario written and discarded, here it is. It's offered in two versions, one with Aircraft Damage enabled that requires &lt;FONT color=#ff0000&gt;Chains of War DLC&lt;/FONT&gt; installed and another without A/C damage that does not. The scenario begins at the same date and time as both &lt;EM&gt;Wargasm 1962&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;Deter, Detect, Defend 1962&lt;/EM&gt; and represents the same conflict only now you control the RAF strategic nuclear forces.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The V-Force represented here is not entirely accurate although the bases and squadron locations are historically correct for 1962.&amp;nbsp;The seven bombers per squadron is conjecture based in part on flight-line photos and&amp;nbsp;dividing the estimated production runs to date by the number of alert squadrons. I have given the Player more Vulcan B.1A variants than actually existed. At this time, the B.2 was still rolling off the production line and some of the B.1s were being upgraded with advanced electronic countermeasures almost equal to the B.2 but only 24-aircraft would receive the upgrade. Rather than sticking the Player with the vulnerable B.1, &lt;EM&gt;83&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;617 RAF&lt;/EM&gt; have been equipped with the B.1A. Substituting the &lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;WE.177&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; loadouts in place of US &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Mk-28&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; probably provides more capability than Bomber Command had in 1962. The V-Bombers&amp;nbsp;carried&amp;nbsp;a much lower&amp;nbsp;yield than their USAF rivals. One B-52G could, in theory deliver 6.8 MT to six targets while the Vulcan B.2 could&amp;nbsp;carry&amp;nbsp;two &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Yellow Sun&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; (only one in the Victor and Vulcan B.1A) or two &lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Red Beard&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; totalling 2 MT&amp;nbsp;or 30 KT respectively. Starting in 1963 with the deployment of &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;Blue Steel&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;, Bomber Command disbanded the &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Thor&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; squadrons and adopted a low altitude attack profile&amp;nbsp;for which&amp;nbsp;the Victors were unsuited. With the 1969 arrival of &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Polaris&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; in the Royal Navy the RAF lost&amp;nbsp;its strategic deterrence mission; Victors replaced Valiants in the tanker role and the Vulcans were&amp;nbsp;given maritime strike tasks&amp;nbsp;in addition to conventional bombing.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;As originally planned, the Player&amp;nbsp;assets were not going to include the RAF's &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;PGM-17 Thor&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;/I&gt;IRBM&amp;nbsp;force but they appear to have been an integral part of the V-Force attack plans and so leaving them out seemed unreasonable. This scenario-creep&amp;nbsp;greatly increased the workload in building &lt;EM&gt;The&lt;/EM&gt; &lt;EM&gt;V-Bombers&lt;/EM&gt; as it became necessary to develop some 60-targets even&amp;nbsp;before creating the targets for the Player's Victors and Vulcans, which is really the reason for the scenario. This and producing the 59-ready events with the associated triggers and actions took a lot of time and while there may be a more elegant solution using Lua scripts it is far beyond my vestigial Lua skills to produce.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;With a launch failure rate of about one-in-four&amp;nbsp;&lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thor&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; seems to have had reliability issues and the evidence suggested that few could meet the readiness required by the QRA.&amp;nbsp;Every operational missile&amp;nbsp;will generate a random ready time from the scenario start;&amp;nbsp;some will ready from between 13 and 34 minutes, &amp;nbsp;others&amp;nbsp;will ready from 35 to 179 minutes with the remainder taking&amp;nbsp;3-hours and longer while a few&amp;nbsp;may never ready for the duration of the scenario. One source consulted mentioned a LOX shortage in the UK about this time (apparently due to the NHS!) and the &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thor&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; required liquid oxygen as part of the fueling process. Be sure to have&amp;nbsp;Raise Popup for special messages checked in the log as each missile will generate a message that will allow you&amp;nbsp;pause and launch. Each of the RAF bunkers is surrounded by three launchers that&amp;nbsp;will spawn and appear in the game&amp;nbsp;when ready to fly. One missile&amp;nbsp;at&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;&lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thor&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; missile school,&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;RAF Feltwell &lt;/EM&gt;had been converted into a training round and was non-servicable so you will&amp;nbsp;have perhaps 59 operational missiles. The British government did not have full launch control of the RAF's &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Thor&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; missile force. USAF personnel from SAC were posted to the RAF&amp;nbsp;squadrons as warhead custodians and to provide the launch keys on orders from SAC headquarters in Kansas.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Testing indicates that CMANO &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Thor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;malfunctions occur at the sharp end so&amp;nbsp;between 20% and 30% of the missiles may be expected to malfunction at the target.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;RAF strategic targeting had been fully integrated into the US SIOP by this time. Unlike the&amp;nbsp; American ICBM force, the RAF &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thors&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; may have been targeted at air-defence&amp;nbsp;bases to facilitate penetration of the V-Bombers into Soviet airspace. It appears that cities were to be attacked as high priority targets since it was anticipated that British urban centres would be hit hard by the many Strategic Rocket Forces (RSVN) &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;SS-4&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;I&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;SS-5&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/I&gt; missiles based in&amp;nbsp;Eastern Europe. Sort of an "I-thought-he-was-going-to-hit-me-so-I-hit-him-back-first" strategy. That said, the evidence suggests that the Soviets employed an almost exclusively countervalue target strategy for their nuclear rocket forces but almost certainly at least some bases in the UK would be attacked. Scoring these scenarios is never easy and while this is not a situation that can have a "winner" in any reasonable sense the Community seems to like some sort of scoring regime. The Player gets points for destroying cities (not defences or IRBM bases)&amp;nbsp;and loses them as Soviet missiles eradicate British cities. Your only defence is to locate and destroy the RSVN installations before their missiles can be launched. Some Soviet missiles'&amp;nbsp;strike missions are inactive and will activate over a longer time frame than your &lt;EM&gt;&lt;B&gt;Thors&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;. This gives you a shot at killing the launchers but you may also destroy them after their missiles have flown, which is part of the problem with a counter-force strategy. Some&amp;nbsp; may be targeting your Bomber Command bases and diversion airfields so be warned.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;As a convenience, Quick Jump slot #1 has been set up on RAF Station Polebrook at a zoom level that includes all of the Player bases with slot #2 set up to cover most of the western Soviet Union where most of your targets are located.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Please post comments and suggestions on the Matrix CMANO forums and thanks for trying &lt;EM&gt;The V-Bombers&lt;/EM&gt;.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.07in; MARGIN-TOP: 0.07in; LINE-HEIGHT: 100%"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Christopher Comars, aka Randomizer&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
  <Complexity>4</Complexity>
  <Difficulty>4</Difficulty>
  <ScenSetting>Northern Europe</ScenSetting>
